  {
   "id": "seg-01",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "Week four. A user reports a strange problem. We discuss the risk around the exception. I document the stack trace so the team can review it later. If the issue template fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the steps to reproduce first. I build a full answer around the pattern: I'm calling about ... Before we move on, Maria says, \"My order hasn't arrived.\" The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "tts": "Week four. A user reports a strange problem. We discuss the risk around the exception. I document the stack trace so the team can review it later. If the issue template fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the steps to reproduce first. I build a full answer around the pattern: I'm calling about  Before we move on, Maria says, \"My order hasn't arrived.\" The team agrees on the plan, and I record the decision.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-01.mp3",
   "zh": "第四周。一位用户报告了一个奇怪的问题。我们讨论了异常相关的风险。我把堆栈跟踪写成文档，方便团队之后查看。如果问题单模板失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。我建议我们先检查复现步骤。我围绕这个句型组织了一个完整的回答：我打电话是想咨询……继续之前，Maria说：\"我的订单还没有到。\"团队就计划达成一致，我记录了决定。",
   "hard": [
    {
     "w": "exception",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "异常，程序运行时发生的特殊错误情况"
    },
    {
     "w": "stack trace",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "堆栈跟踪，显示错误经过哪些函数调用的记录"
    },
    {
     "w": "I'm calling about ...",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我打电话是想咨询……"
    },
    {
     "w": "My order hasn't arrived.",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "我的订单还没有到。"
    },
    {
     "w": "issue template",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "问题单模板，指导用户提供必要信息的格式"
    },
    {
     "w": "steps to reproduce",
     "type": "term",
     "def": "复现步骤，能够再次触发问题的操作顺序"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "seg-02",
   "spk": "Alex",
   "en": "My package is late. I call customer service. Priya checks with me, \"Could you check the status?\" I answer clearly, \"The problem started yesterday.\" If the error type fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the line number first. The result depends on the expected behavior, so I check it twice. I explain the actual behavior to a new teammate. The day ends with a clear plan for tomorrow.",
   "tts": "My package is late. I call customer service. Priya checks with me, \"Could you check the status?\" I answer clearly, \"The problem started yesterday.\" If the error type fails, we need a clear plan. I suggest that we check the line number first. The result depends on the expected behavior, so I check it twice. I explain the actual behavior to a new teammate. The day ends with a clear plan for tomorrow.",
   "audio_file": "audio/seg-02.mp3",
   "zh": "我的包裹迟到了。我打了客服电话。Priya向我确认：\"你可以查询一下状态吗？\"我清楚地回答：\"问题从昨天开始。\"如果错误类型失败，我们需要一个清晰的方案。我建议我们先检查行号。结果取决于预期行为，所以我检查了两遍。我向一位新队友解释了实际行为。这一天以一份清晰的明日计划结束。",
   "hard": [
    {
